WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.635
Credit card skimming

00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:03.144
scripts using WebRTC

00:00:02.956 --> 00:00:03.651
found

00:00:04.182 --> 00:00:06.068
Researchers found credit-card

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.071
skimming scripts on

00:00:06.882 --> 00:00:08.368
popular shopping sites

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.370
that steal payment

00:00:09.182 --> 00:00:10.278
data and send

00:00:10.090 --> 00:00:10.750
it out over

00:00:10.562 --> 00:00:11.528
WebRTC

00:00:11.765 --> 00:00:12.590
a channel that

00:00:12.401 --> 00:00:13.733
slips past many

00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:14.488
blocklists

00:00:15.022 --> 00:00:16.354
Lascana replied to

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:17.309
us and removed

00:00:17.121 --> 00:00:18.182
the Quorum pixel

00:00:17.994 --> 00:00:18.866
from their site

00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:20.753
by November 24th at

00:00:20.564 --> 00:00:23.241
15:48 UTC

00:00:23.774 --> 00:00:24.894
Only step 4

00:00:24.706 --> 00:00:25.696
is an ordinary

00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:26.427
web request

00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:27.807
which a connect-src

00:00:27.618 --> 00:00:28.573
rule can block

00:00:28.774 --> 00:00:29.682
steps 5 to

00:00:29.493 --> 00:00:30.483
7 run over

00:00:30.295 --> 00:00:31.498
the WebRTC data

00:00:31.309 --> 00:00:31.922
channel

00:00:32.111 --> 00:00:33.832
outside connect-src

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.364
Full story on

00:00:35.175 --> 00:00:36.071
the dashboard
